<article class="env-lemma" id="0BT3">
  <p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/0BT3">Lemma <span data-tag="0BT3">49.2.5</span>.</a> If $A \to A_1$ is flat, then the base change map (<a href="/tag/0BVB" data-tag="0BVB">49.2.3.1</a>) induces an isomorphism $\omega _{B/A} \otimes _ B B_1 \to \omega _{B_1/A_1}$. </p>
</article><article class="env-proof">
    <p>
      <strong>Proof.</strong>
      Assume that $A \to A_1$ is flat. By construction of $\omega _{B/A}$ we may assume that $A \to B$ is finite. Then $\omega _{B/A} = \mathop{\mathrm{Hom}}\nolimits _ A(B, A)$ and $\omega _{B_1/A_1} = \mathop{\mathrm{Hom}}\nolimits _{A_1}(B_1, A_1)$. Since $B_1 = B \otimes _ A A_1$ the result follows from More on Algebra, Lemma <a href="/tag/087R" data-tag="087R">15.67.4</a>. 
      <span class="qed">$\square$</span>
    </p>
</article>